{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model capability cost and latency tradeoff model capability cost and latency tradeoff","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","fileName":"Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering","Task-Specific Network Prompt","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model capability cost and latency tradeoff model capability cost and latency tradeoff","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","fileName":"Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff","heading":"Model Capability Cost and Latency Tradeoff","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A network AI model should be selected for the work it must perform rather than by size or reputation alone. Complex troubleshooting may justify a slower, more capable model, while routine classification or formatting may be served by a smaller model with lower latency and token cost.\n\nThe tradeoff must be measured on representative network questions. A fast answer that invents syntax is expensive in operational terms, while a high-quality answer whose